# Two kinds of case, both taken from what real search actually returned (evals/probes).
# Wrong subject: a name collision that grounds a fluent card in the wrong thing.
# Tooling around the subject: genuinely about the technology, and still the wrong source.
#
# `identity` is what the deterministic name gate matches against, and is NOT the title:
# GitHub carries the repository name there and the full name as the title. The first eval
# run conflated them and scored the resulting gate rejections as model failures.
